  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot t+(-1)\\cdot (t+1)=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere all three coefficients are nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n2t+1=0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot t+1\\cdot (t+1).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
